From 4300afca1a7633df7f988958424bc7b6dd29c4f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:21:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] FX: restore Melodee's per-track audio inserts

Each track's three slots take any shared-rack audio effect again (drive,
crush, phaser, flanger, chorus and so on) as well as the note effects,
run in series on the track before its level, pan and shared sends.
This undoes the effects part of upstream 0e3d353 ("simplify FX
routing"), Melodee's own tested insert code, with two adjustments:

- The shared rack keeps states 0..2; each track's three follow
  (FX_TRACK_SI). The states live in the pool, not ordinary RAM.
- One REVERB across the racks, as before: choosing it in a track's slot
  or a shared slot turns it off where it was.

A silent track's inserts are also given back when they go off or reach
MIX 0. Older projects' per-track audio effects load again. Buffers come
from the on-demand memory arena.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
